 how can LLMs be used to innovate math learning in schools and universities?": "LLMs could personalize feedback (e.g., step-by-step errors) and explain proofs intuitively. Interactive examples like ‘“Why did this variable fail here?”’—combined with gamification—could make abstract concepts tangible for students, especially those from diverse backgrounds."
